ken@isgtec.com (Ken Newman) writes:
>One thing that has been annoying me while I am getting into nethack is
>when you have a large pile of junk on the ground, by killing a lot of
>monsters in one spot, or in various other ways, and you want one item
>at the bottom or in the middle. Is there an easy way to sift through
>10 or 15 items without a) picking them all up, or b) kicking single
>items off the top? Method b takes forever, and you run the risk of
>breaking fragile things. Also, what do you do when you kill a real heavy
>monster, like an owlbear, he drops something good, and then falls on it?
>If you can't pick him up, or kick him over, are you just s.o.l.?
>Or is my character just not strong enough?

When a situation like this arises, move onto the pile with pickup off.
(Use "@" or "m".)  Then use ":" to see all of what's in the pile.  When
you spot something you want to pick up, then use the command "," to pick
something up where you're standing.  If there is more than one class of
item in the pile, the game will prompt you for what classes of items you
want to pick up.  (E.g. if there is armor, food, and weapons, enter "%"
to pick up the food.)  Then the game will ask you one by one what specific
items of those class(es) you chose you want to pick up.  "y" to pick it
up, "n" not to, "a" to pick up all items of that class in the pile, or "q"
to quit going through the pile.
Hope this helps.  Happy hacking!
